New Zealand's 30-man squad for the 2011 Rugby World Cup was announced on 23 August.<ref>{{cite news |title=Vito sneaks into World Cup 30 |url=http://www.planetrugby.com/story/0,25883,3562_7118969,00.html |publisher=Planet Rugby |date=23 August 2011 |access-date=9 September 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110923033400/http://www.planetrugby.com/story/0,25883,3562_7118969,00.html |archive-date=23 September 2011 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

On 1 October, [[Dan Carter]] sustained a tournament-ending groin injury and was replaced in the squad by Aaron Cruden.<ref>{{cite news |title=All Blacks' worst fears confirmed |url=http://www.nzherald.co.nz/rugby-world-cup-2011/news/article.cfm?c_id=522&objectid=10755991 |work=The New Zealand Herald |date=1 October 2011 }}</ref>

On 9 October, [[Mils Muliaina]] sustained a shoulder fracture and [[Colin Slade]] suffered a groin tear. Stephen Donald and Hosea Gear were called into the squad to replace them.<ref>{{cite news |title=All Blacks: Donald & Gear called up |url=http://www.nzherald.co.nz/sport/news/article.cfm?c_id=4&objectid=10758055 |work=The New Zealand Herald |date=1 October 2011 }}</ref>

Squad and caps are current as of 10 October 2011.

