Taylor Paris of [[Canada national rugby union team|Canada]] was the youngest player named to a squad at 18, while [[Russia national rugby union team|Russia]]'s Viacheslav Grachev, 38, was the oldest. However, Paris did not appear in any of Canada's matches,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.espnscrum.com/statsguru/rugby/player/128737.html?class=1;template=results;type=player;view=match |title=Statsguru / Player analysis / Taylor Paris / Test matches |work=ESPN Scrum |access-date=21 October 2011 }}</ref> making Wales' 19-year-old [[George North]] the youngest to actually appear in the World Cup.

